   "text": "You don't need a perfect resume, you need one clear sentence. When someone asks what you do,"
  },
  {
   "s": 4.58,
   "e": 9.08,
   "text": "most people say a job title and then they ramble. Marketing, I guess a bit of everything,"
  },
  {
   "s": 9.22,
   "e": 14.24,
   "text": "it kind of depends. The other person nods and forgets it by lunch. So write one sentence with"
  },
  {
   "s": 14.24,
   "e": 19.32,
   "text": "three parts, who you help what you help them do and your proof. For example, I help local cafes"
  },
  {
   "s": 19.32,
   "e": 24.74,
   "text": "fill their quiet weekday hours, proven by a loyalty card that brought one cafe 30 new regulars."
  },
  {
   "s": 25.22,
   "e": 29.38,
   "text": "Or for a developer, I help small clinics cut missed appointments with text reminders,"
  },
  {
   "s": 29.38,
   "e": 34.9,
   "text": "proven by the system I built for my dentist. Then put it everywhere, your profile headline,"
  },
  {
   "s": 35.1,
   "e": 39.14,
   "text": "the top of your resume and the first line of every message you send. Here's the test,"
  },
  {
   "s": 39.3,
   "e": 44.0,
   "text": "read it to a friend and ask them to say it back. If they can't repeat it, cut words until they can."
  },
  {
   "s": 44.58,
   "e": 48.94,
   "text": "Write yours right now in under 25 words, who you help what you do and your proof."
